agram:\n- \\( Z_1 = 150 \\, \\text{ft} \\)\n- \\( Z_2 = 25 \\, \\text{ft}", "The question asks which graph best represents Hermann Ebbinghaus's findings on memory retention over time. Ebbinghaus is famous for his work on the forgetting curve, which shows that memory retention declines rapidly after learning and then levels off over time. This is typically represented by a curve that starts high and slopes downward, often resembling a bell-shaped curve that is steeper at the beginning and flattens out.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\n- (A) is a horizontal line, suggesting no change over time \u2014 incorrect.\n- (B) is a bell-shaped curve peaking in the middle \u2014 this is more typical of a normal distribution, not"], "errors": ["", "", "", "", ""], "mean_ttft_ms": 92485.31381340002, "median_ttft_ms": 141080.77230800007, "std_ttft_ms": 67985.80973068286, "p99_ttft_ms": 155067.12601108002, "mean_tpot_ms": 414.82930932913297, "median_tpot_ms": 208.75865228346424, "std_tpot_ms": 386.059192042227, "p99_tpot_ms": 1135.8390686195273, "mean_itl_ms": 452.0772781698113, "median_itl_ms": 137.02201399996738, "std_itl_ms": 4027.513644526585, "p99_itl_ms": 977.170235240006}